7d9eee22256a5469c6746a0f2a7901f00","event_uuid":"58e5e5fc-8894-4a36-893c-57314b86f163","position":{"commit_sha":"c8d3b38441bde26f8114ad87e01b5a0bf262edd0","position":"1789021269301742001-58e5e5fc-8894-4a36-893c-57314b86f163"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed through Gerrit change 2952.\n\nEvidence:\n- Plan review passed and ticket was claimed before code work.\n- Commit `35e6e5714c0b2b3ad03cc8464d2d969c97c1f068` merged to `origin/main` with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and `0` unresolved comments.\n- Local validation before push: targeted MCP/doctor/config tests passed (`32 passed, 3 skipped` after the final review fix); `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed; `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` passed. Full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` was attempted earlier and completed only to unrelated local/baseline/environment failures documented in the session log, while Gerrit Verified passed on the submitted patchset.\n- Project config verification from merged worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/mcp-project-bubblefish`: `codex mcp get rebar` resolves repo config using `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; `copilot mcp list` shows `rebar` under workspace/repository-scoped servers, not user servers.\n- Machine-local cutover completed after merge: removed `rebar` from `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` (kept `atlassian`, `serena`); removed global `mcpServers.rebar` from `~/.claude.json` without touching `projects.*`; removed `[mcp_servers.rebar]` from `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n- Non-project verification from `/Users/joeoakhart`: `codex mcp get rebar` reports no server named `rebar`; `copilot mcp list` shows only user `serena` and `atlassian`; global Claude config has no `mcpServers.rebar`.\n- Requested `~/rebar` verification note: `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` is intentionally read-only for this session and is currently behind `origin/main`, so it does not yet contain the merged `.mcp.json`; I did not modify it. The merged project worktree verification above exercises the landed repo config.\n\nDocs touched: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, `docs/mcp-auth.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/README.md`, example client config files, and `mcp-clients.local.example.json`.","timestamp":1789017238111018001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788982178223188001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3be036c5-394b-4c78-9892-3757e2d72248","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"05e9-2d68-5efd-45d1"},{"link_uuid":"b13dd049-7c1e-43d7-86e3-d64642bf13b6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8fc2-f1ea-68d5-4545"},{"link_uuid":"5941b51c-99de-4519-b535-822d193f50f4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8fad-2fa0-c63a-4815"},{"link_uuid":"5d744b2f-b86d-4066-b647-d74e0c386088","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c392-e6e1-62f1-477b"}],"description":"## Problem\nrebar MCP is configured globally per machine for all 3 harnesses, so every codex/claude/copilot session on the host gets it, and codex startup failed (2026-09-09) with a not-logged-in error when a GUI-launched process lacked MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX (valid PAT; 401 rendered as not-logged-in). Operator ruling: scope rebar MCP to this project via harness-native project mechanisms; claude+copilot consolidate onto one PAT var.\n\n## Plan (tracked-file half; machine-local half already applied)\n1. Add .mcp.json at repo root: rebar server entry, type http, url https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/, header Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI}. Read by Claude Code (project scope) AND Copilot CLI >=1.0.83 (workspace config; verified it loads .mcp.json first-found over .github/mcp.json and overrides user-level entries).\n2. Add [mcp_servers.rebar] to tracked .codex/config.toml: url https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/ + bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\" + startup_timeout_sec = 120 (carry the cold-start comment from the user-level config).\n3. Update infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md: document MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI (claude slot shared by Claude Code + Copilot CLI; codex keeps its own), the launchd-env publishing step (GUI launches do not source ~/.zshenv), and the project-scope files.\n4. If mcp-clients.local.example.json or docs/mcp-client-setup.md reference the old per-client global wiring, update the affected lines.\n\n\n## Established operator evidence / implementation notes\n- Do not re-derive: Copilot CLI 1.0.83 was empirically verified to load workspace `.mcp.json` first-found, ignore `.github/mcp.json` when present, and let workspace entries override user-level entries.\n- Do not re-derive: Claude Code reads `.mcp.json` as project scope and expands `${VAR}` in headers. The shared `.mcp.json` will therefore use the braced `${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI}` spelling and the post-merge verification must exercise a real Copilot CLI listing from `~/rebar` with the machine-local `launchctl` environment already published.\n- Do not re-derive: Codex reads tracked `.codex/config.toml`; the existing machine-local block already used `startup_timeout_sec = 120`, so the tracked project block carries the same key.\n- Operator ruling: Claude Code and Copilot CLI consolidate onto `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI`, a machine-local alias whose VALUE is the existing `/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude` / `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE` slot; Codex keeps `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; no server-side SSM/keychain slot changes are in scope. The server authenticates the bearer value against the existing `claude` static-token digest record; there is no server-side `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` token_env record and the old copilot server slot remains populated but unused by the new project config.\n- Related consumer/doc surfaces to update or verify: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/README.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/claude/.mcp.json`, `examples/mcp-clients/copilot/mcp-config.json`, `examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml`, `mcp-clients.local.example.json`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py`, and `tests/scripts/test_mcp_client_pats.py`.\n- Machine-local cutover is expand/contract: first verify project-scope rebar resolves while global config still exists; then remove only global `rebar` entries; back-out is to restore the saved user-level rebar entry if project resolution regresses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `.mcp.json` and `.codex/config.toml` define project-scope rebar MCP entries with env-var references only and URL `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/`; no secret values are committed; targeted tests prove the committed config resolves to accepted loopback bearers and rejects absent/wrong bearers.\n- [x] Claude Code and Copilot CLI use `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` for the shared project-scope rebar entry, while Codex uses `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; no server-side SSM slot changes are made, and docs explain `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` is a local alias to the existing claude PAT value/server digest.\n- [x] `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md` documents the CLI-PAT consolidation, launchd environment publishing for GUI-launched processes, and project-scope config files.\n- [x] Existing setup docs/examples/tests that encode the old per-client global wiring are updated or explicitly verified as already current, including `docs/mcp-auth.md` if its per-client naming text is affected.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` passes before push.\n- [x] [non-codebase] After merge, machine-local global rebar MCP entries are removed from Copilot, Claude, and Codex configs while keeping unrelated servers; first verify project-scope resolution while global exists, then verify project and non-project resolution after cutover, including actual rebar server listing/connection rather than config presence only, and record the host-local evidence in a ticket comment before close.\n  provenance: environment=operator-workstation; principal=configured-local-user; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — ran Codex and Copilot MCP client commands plus static Claude global-config check after removing user-level rebar entries; evidence recorded in ticket comment.\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Run targeted config/documentation checks while implementing as needed.\n- Before Gerrit push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` from the fresh worktree.\n- Server-side auth proof: targeted tests model `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLI` as carrying the same value as the existing claude PAT record, so Copilot/Claude requests authenticate against the existing server-side `claude` digest without adding an SSM slot; Codex authenticates against the existing codex digest.\n- After merge and machine-local cutover, verify from `~/rebar`: `codex mcp get rebar`, `copilot mcp list`, and Claude project config resolution via `.mcp.json`; from a non-project directory (`~`), verify rebar is absent from global Codex/Copilot/Claude config surfaces.\n\n## File impact\n.mcp.json, .codex/config.toml, infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md, docs/mcp-client-setup.md (maybe), mcp-clients.local.example.json (maybe)","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".mcp.json","reason":"project-scope Claude/Copilot rebar MCP config"},{"path":".codex/config.toml","reason":"project-scope Codex rebar MCP config"},{"path":"docs/mcp-auth.md","reason":"document server-side PAT slots versus client-side CLI alias"},{"path":"docs/mcp-client-setup.md","reason":"document project-scoped MCP client setup"